6. LINEAR QUEUE USING ARRAY
============================================================

In Linear Queue:

1. Insertion takes place from REAR.
2. Deletion takes place from FRONT.
3. It follows FIFO.

We maintain:

front = -1
rear = -1

Initially both pointers are -1.


A. INSERTION (ENQUEUE)

STEPS:

1. Check whether rear == capacity - 1.
   If true, queue is full.

2. If front == -1:
   It means queue is empty.
   Set front = 0.

3. Increase rear by 1.

4. Insert the element at arr[rear].


EXAMPLE:

Capacity = 5

Initially:

Index:       0      1      2      3      4
           +------+------+------+------+------+
Array:     |      |      |      |      |      |
           +------+------+------+------+------+

front = -1
rear = -1


Insert 10, 20, 30:

Index:       0      1      2      3      4
           +------+------+------+------+------+
Array:     |  10  |  20  |  30  |      |      |
           +------+------+------+------+------+
              ^             ^
            FRONT          REAR


B. DELETION (DEQUEUE)

STEPS:

1. Check whether front == -1.
   If true, queue is empty.

2. Store arr[front] in removedElement.

3. If front == rear:
   Only one element is present.
   Set front = rear = -1.

4. Otherwise:
   Increase front by 1.

5. Return removedElement.


EXAMPLE:

Before:

Index:       0      1      2      3      4
           +------+------+------+------+------+
Array:     |  10  |  20  |  30  |      |      |
           +------+------+------+------+------+
              ^             ^
            FRONT          REAR

Delete 10:

After:

Index:       0      1      2      3      4
           +------+------+------+------+------+
Array:     |  10  |  20  |  30  |      |      |
           +------+------+------+------+------+
                     ^      ^
                   FRONT   REAR

IMPORTANT:

The value 10 may still physically exist in the array.

But it is logically deleted because front moved forward.


C. PROBLEM WITH LINEAR QUEUE

Capacity = 5

Insert:

10, 20, 30, 40, 50

Index:       0      1      2      3      4
           +------+------+------+------+------+
Array:     |  10  |  20  |  30  |  40  |  50  |
           +------+------+------+------+------+
              ^                           ^
            FRONT                       REAR

Delete:

10, 20, 30

Index:       0      1      2      3      4
           +------+------+------+------+------+
Array:     |  10  |  20  |  30  |  40  |  50  |
           +------+------+------+------+------+
                                   ^      ^
                                 FRONT   REAR

Now rear == capacity - 1.

We cannot insert another element.

But indexes 0, 1 and 2 are logically empty.

This problem is called FALSE OVERFLOW.

SOLUTION:

Use Circular Queue.


TIME COMPLEXITY:

Enqueue = O(1)
Dequeue = O(1)
Peek = O(1)
Display = O(n)


