============================================================

1. CPU Scheduling
   Processes wait in a queue for CPU execution.

2. Printer Scheduling
   Print jobs are processed in order.

3. BFS (Breadth First Search)
   Queue is used to visit nodes level by level.

4. Network Data Packets
   Packets wait in queues before processing.

5. Call Center Systems
   Customers wait for their turn.

6. Keyboard Buffer
   Input characters can be stored in a queue.

7. Task Scheduling
   Tasks wait until they are ready for execution.

8. Message Queues
   Used for communication between systems.

9. Priority Scheduling
   Higher-priority tasks are processed first.

10. Dijkstra's Algorithm
    A Priority Queue is used to select the vertex
    with the minimum tentative distance.

11. Sliding Window Problems
    Deque is used to maintain maximum or minimum
    elements in a sliding window.

12. Level Order Traversal
    Queue is used in Binary Tree traversal.


